LAST_SUCCESS=Task 90 M1 NOW FULLY BINDER (no ip shell-outs) + device-verified. Root cause of the blocker found by isolated test: rsbinder-aidl wrongly treated @JavaOnlyImmutable as Java-only (starts_with("@JavaOnly")) → empty UidRangeParcel struct. Fixed (1 line, ends_with("StableParcelable")) in the rsbinder fork (submodule external/rsbinder, branch RENAMED wart-recursive→wandr-recursive, commit eccc077, pushed). Repointed wandr-hal-net to vendored external/rsbinder (was git pin; now matches wandr-host). With UidRangeParcel fields, networkAddUidRanges(0..99999) works → netd installs uidrange rules (incl 29000: fwmark 0x0 all-uids→wlan0) → replaces the catch-all `ip rule from all lookup`. Dropped install_default_rule + apply_address(ip) + run_ip from lib.rs. Device-verified WITHOUT the ip rule: ping 0%, curl http 301, curl https://codeberg.org 200 (DNS+TLS). wandr-host runs as ROOT (uid 0) so the uid-1000 test failures earlier were a red herring (inet-group/firewall, not routing).
NOTES=M1 + M2(scan/connect engine) DONE. MANUAL STEP NEEDED: set default branch of codeberg harryzz/rsbinder to wandr-recursive (UI), then wart-recursive deletable (pre-receive hook blocks deleting the default branch). Remaining task-90: M2 host WIT (wifi-host) + privilege gate + arbiter relay, M3 saved-networks, M4 settings app. Only non-binder bit left in M1 = DHCP (raw socket, root, irreducible).
